# Project Rules

## Stack
- React + Vite
- Mantine for UI components — use Mantine components before writing custom CSS
- No additional UI libraries or CSS frameworks without asking first (no Tailwind, no MUI, etc.)
- No state management libraries (Redux, Zustand, etc.) — use React's built-in useState/useContext unless truly needed

## Code style
- Functional components with hooks only
- Keep components small — if a component file passes ~150 lines, suggest splitting it, don't just let it grow
- Prefer boring, well-known patterns over clever ones
- Comment non-obvious logic, skip comments on self-explanatory code

## Constraints
- Don't add npm packages without asking first and explaining why
- Don't introduce backend/database/auth unless explicitly requested — this is a static portfolio site
- No animation libraries (Framer Motion, GSAP) unless asked — Mantine's built-in transitions are enough for now
- Explain any pattern that isn't plain React + Mantine before using it

## Priorities
1. Working and simple over impressive and complex
2. Code I can read and explain over code that's "elegant"
3. Consistency across files over one-off clever solutions